    ancientSymbolism: ["Across cultures, teeth have carried associations with strength, maturity, appearance, speech, and the ability to take in and process experience. Losing them can create an image of transition: something familiar no longer feels as stable as it once did.", "Folk traditions offer many different readings of tooth-loss dreams, sometimes linking them with worry, change, family, or fortune. These are cultural stories rather than predictions, and they are most useful when they open a question instead of closing it."],
