    metaDescription: "What does a falling dream mean? Explore falling from a height, waking before landing, fear, loss of control, symbolism, psychology, and personal context.",
    h1: "Falling Dream Meaning",
    intro: "Dreaming about falling can feel so physical that you wake with a jolt. The dream may bring uncertainty, lost support, pressure, surrender, or a change that is moving faster than you feel ready for into focus. Where you fell from, whether you landed, and what you felt are more useful than one fixed interpretation.",
    ancientSymbolism: ["Across stories and symbolic traditions, descent has often marked a passage from certainty into the unknown. Falling can represent a loss of status or control, but it can also picture surrender: the moment when an old position can no longer be maintained.", "These cultural echoes are not predictions. They offer a way to ask what currently feels unstable, humbling, or beyond your ability to control—and what kind of support could help you meet it."],
    jungianPerspective: ["From a Jungian-inspired perspective, a falling dream may dramatize tension between the identity you try to maintain and feelings that pull you back toward vulnerability, limits, or neglected needs. The fall can interrupt a sense of being fully in control.", "The dream changes when falling feels peaceful rather than frightening. Fear may point toward instability or performance pressure, while relief can suggest a wish to stop holding everything up. A physical sleep start can also enter dream imagery, so symbolism is only one possible lens."],
    personalContext: ["Begin with the moment before the fall. Were you climbing, flying, standing near an edge, pushed by someone, or walking on ground that gave way? That scene may resemble the area of life where confidence, trust, pace, or support currently feels uncertain.", "Then notice what happened next. Waking before landing can leave the situation unresolved; landing safely can introduce resilience; continuing to fall can reflect a problem that still feels difficult to contain. Your own associations and current circumstances give the dream its personal meaning."],
    commonScenarios: [{ title: "What does it mean when you dream about falling?", copy: "A general falling dream may bring loss of control, uncertainty, pressure, or the need for support into focus. Ask what was happening immediately before the fall and whether the strongest feeling was fear, surprise, relief, or freedom." }, { title: "Falling from a high place", copy: "Height can amplify exposure, ambition, responsibility, or fear of failure. Consider what you have worked hard to reach and what currently makes that position feel difficult to sustain." }, { title: "Falling and waking up before landing", copy: "Waking before impact can leave the dream emotionally unfinished. It may mirror an unresolved decision or uncertain outcome, though a normal physical sleep start can also shape this experience." }, { title: "Falling while flying", copy: "A fall after flying can turn freedom into a question about sustainability. Reflect on what changed just before you lost height and whether a new opportunity also carries pressure to keep performing." }],
