    keyword: "dream about ex meaning",
    title: "Dreaming About Your Ex Meaning",
    metaTitle: "Why Do I Keep Dreaming About My Ex? Meaning & Reflection",
    metaDescription: "Why do you keep dreaming about your ex? Explore reunion dreams, an ex with someone else, recurring dreams, relationship context, psychology, and personal meaning.",
    h1: "Why Do I Keep Dreaming About My Ex?",
    intro: "Dreaming about an ex can bring back tenderness, anger, longing, embarrassment, or confusion—even when you have no wish to restart the relationship. The dream does not prove that your ex is thinking about you or that you should contact them. It may instead connect a present feeling with a person, relationship pattern, or earlier version of yourself stored strongly in memory.",
    ancientSymbolism: ["Older stories often use a returning figure from the past as a symbol of unfinished promises, remembered lessons, or a former identity asking to be reconsidered. The return does not always call for reunion; sometimes it marks the distance between who a person was and who they are becoming.", "Relationship traditions vary widely, and none can establish what another person feels. Their value here is metaphorical: what quality, need, conflict, or life chapter does your ex represent to you now?"],
    jungianPerspective: ["From a Jungian-inspired perspective, a person in a dream can carry both their real history and qualities the dreamer associates with them. An ex may represent attachment, rejection, freedom, conflict, youth, confidence, or a part of yourself that became more visible during that relationship.", "Recurring dreams do not automatically mean unresolved romantic desire. They may appear when a current relationship, transition, or emotional situation resembles an older pattern. The action and emotional tone of the dream are more informative than the ex's presence alone."],
    personalContext: ["Start with what happened between you in the dream. A calm conversation, another breakup, an apology, an argument, or seeing your ex with someone else can each connect with a different present concern. Ask what feeling followed you into the morning.", "Then consider what has changed recently. A new relationship, loneliness, an anniversary, social comparison, renewed confidence, or a difficult conversation can activate memories without being a message to act. If the past relationship involved harm, prioritize present safety and support rather than using the dream to justify contact."],
    commonScenarios: [{ title: "Why do I keep dreaming about my ex?", copy: "Recurring dreams about an ex may reflect a repeated emotional pattern, a current situation that resembles the past, or memories that still carry strong feeling. Recurrence alone does not mean you want the relationship back." }, { title: "Dreaming about getting back together with your ex", copy: "A reunion may represent longing for the person, but it can also point toward familiarity, reassurance, intimacy, or a quality of your former self that you miss. Notice what the reunion gave you emotionally." }, { title: "Dreaming about your ex with someone else", copy: "This scene can bring comparison, replacement, grief, jealousy, or self-worth into focus. It is not evidence of what your ex is actually doing; ask which part of the scene felt most personal." }, { title: "Dreaming about an ex while in a relationship", copy: "An ex appearing during a current relationship does not by itself signal disloyalty or dissatisfaction. The dream may be comparing patterns, processing memory, or highlighting a need you want to communicate more clearly now." }, { title: "Dreaming about an ex apologizing or talking to you", copy: "A conversation can give the mind a place to rehearse words, closure, or acknowledgment that was missing. Consider whether the message reflects what you needed to hear—or what you are ready to tell yourself." }],
    reflectionQuestions: ["What feeling was strongest when you saw your ex, and did it change after waking?", "What did this person or that period of life represent to you beyond the relationship itself?", "Does anything in your present life resemble the emotional pattern of the dream?", "What need, boundary, or form of closure can you address without assuming the dream tells you to make contact?"],
    relatedDreams: ["recurring-dreams", "dreaming-about-someone", "being-chased", "death", "teeth-falling-out", "pregnancy"],
