    ancientSymbolism: ["In cultural stories, clothing can mark status, role, protection, ceremony, and belonging. Removing it may symbolize loss of position or privacy, but it can also represent honesty, simplicity, renewal, or stepping outside an assigned role.", "Traditions disagree about nakedness, and their meanings reflect different attitudes toward the body, dignity, and community. Treat these associations as context rather than a verdict about your character or future."],
    jungianPerspective: ["From a Jungian-inspired perspective, public nakedness may dramatize tension around the persona—the social face used to meet expectations. Without the usual covering, the dreamer may feel exposed as incomplete, unprepared, or more authentic than feels socially safe.", "Shame is not the only possible meaning. Calm or freedom can suggest relief from performance, while discovering that nobody notices may invite reflection on whether self-judgment is louder than the attention other people actually give."],
    personalContext: ["Consider where you currently feel evaluated: a new role, presentation, relationship, public decision, creative project, or conversation may make ordinary uncertainty feel visible. The setting often identifies the area of pressure.", "Then notice the crowd. Mockery, indifference, support, or your own ability to continue normally each changes the emotional message. Personal and cultural feelings about nudity also matter, so no single interpretation fits everyone."],
    commonScenarios: [{ title: "Being naked and nobody notices", copy: "When nobody reacts, the dream may highlight the gap between how exposed you feel and how closely others are actually watching. It can also reflect loneliness if you wanted someone to notice your distress." }, { title: "Being naked at work or school", copy: "Work and school settings can connect nudity with performance, competence, comparison, or feeling unprepared for evaluation. Ask what task or expectation currently makes you feel visible." }, { title: "Trying to cover yourself or find clothes", copy: "Searching for cover can express a wish to regain privacy, control what others see, or prepare before being evaluated. Notice whether anyone helped and whether you eventually felt safe." }, { title: "Feeling comfortable while naked", copy: "Comfort can shift the dream toward authenticity, self-acceptance, or freedom from a role that feels restrictive. Consider where you want to be less guarded in waking life." }, { title: "Other people stare or laugh", copy: "A reacting crowd may amplify fear of criticism, rejection, or a mistake becoming public. It reflects an emotional concern, not proof of what other people think about you." }],
