    ancientSymbolism: ["Across cultures, weddings mark a witnessed threshold: families, identities, responsibilities, and futures are joined through ritual. The clothing, vows, guests, timing, and community around the couple can be as symbolically important as marriage itself.", "Because wedding customs differ widely, no traditional reading is universal. Cultural symbolism can open useful questions about commitment and belonging without determining what will happen."],
