    jungianPerspective: ["From a Jungian-inspired perspective, an earthquake may dramatize a shift beneath the conscious sense of order. A belief, identity, relationship, or role that once organized life may be changing before the mind has found a new stable structure.", "The dream's setting helps locate the pressure. Shaking ground can emphasize basic trust, a damaged house can bring the inner or family world into focus, and a collapsing public building may point toward work, institutions, or social roles. These are possibilities, not diagnoses or universal definitions."],
